Last Thursday, I had the great privilege of presenting my PhD thesis (in just 5 minutes!) at the annual event organized by the Belgian College of Neuropsychopharmacology and Biological Psychiatry. This was a fantastic opportunity to share my research on the exploration of attentional biases in alcohol use disorders and to discover the work of talented researchers from all over the country.
<br>
I'm deeply honored to have received the Belgium's Got Talent 2024 award, which recognizes innovative contributions in our field. The evening was enriched by very interesting lectures, including a thought-provoking talk by Prof. Siri Leknes on the myths and realities of opioids.
<br>
Thank you to the organizers and the jury for this recognition! 🎉 

